[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Ne7 System"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "development,pawn-chain"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "rare"]
[Opponent "3...Ne7"]
[Start "advance-qb6 3.e5"]

3... Ne7 ( 3... b6 4. c3 { Support d4 first; Black's bishop wants to trade on a6, so we keep it calm. } 4... Qd7 5. Bd3 ) ( 3... Bd7 4. Nf3 { Develop and keep the centre. Black is just losing a tempo with the bishop. } 4... c5 5. c3 Nc6 6. Be2 ) ( 3... f6 $6 4. Bd3 { Develops and prepares Qh5+: if Black takes on e5, the diagonal from h5 to the king is wide open. } 4... fxe5 $2 5. Qh5+ { Check. Black's king cannot castle any more, and the only block, ...g6, loses a pawn. } 5... g6 6. Bxg6+ { Takes a pawn with check and forces the king to d7, where it is stuck in the middle. } 6... Kd7 7. Nf3 ) 4. Nf3 { Develop and guard e5 and d4. No need to commit the c-pawn yet. } 4... Nf5 ( 4... Nbc6 5. Bd3 { The bishop eyes h7, and Black's knights get in each other's way. } ) ( 4... c5 5. c3 Nbc6 6. Na3 { Heads for c2 to guard d4 once more without blocking the c3 pawn. } ) 5. Bd3 { Challenges the knight on f5 and aims at h7. } 5... c5 6. dxc5 { Takes the pawn first: Black's knight left e7 and cannot recapture on c5 with a piece. } 6... Bxc5 7. O-O { Castle before Black gets a free move. } 7... Nc6 8. a3 { Stops ...Nb4 trying to trade our good bishop, and gives the bishop on c1 b2. } 8... Bb6 9. Re1 { Supports the e5 pawn, which Black's pieces will try to hit. } 9... O-O 10. Nc3 { Attacks the d5 pawn, which only the queen guards. [%cal Gc3d5] } 10... h6 11. Bxf5 { Trades our bishop for Black's best minor piece so the e6 pawn can no longer recapture with a piece. } 11... exf5 12. Nxd5 { Wins a pawn: the d5 pawn was guarded only once. Plan: develop, win the isolated pawn, and keep an eye on h7. } *
